.SH NAME
.PP
auto-clean-tmp - Remove old files from tmp directories

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-clean-tmp [days-old]
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
days-old    Optional minimum age of files to remove
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-clean-tmp
command removes old files from tmp directories.  The user can specify
the minimum age of files to be removed, in days.  By default,
files older than 180 days are removed.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-clean-tmp 90
.ad
.fi

.SH FILES
.nf
.na
/tmp, /var/tmp, /usr/tmp
.ad
.fi

